[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z # easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z easy-host is a Linux CLI that turns a git repository into a long-running, self-hosted HTTP service on a single machine. It clones the repository, builds an image with Railpack (no per-repo Dockerfile), runs it under rootless Podman with `--restart=always` on one host port you declare, health-gates every update, keeps the last two images for rollback, and never deletes a named volume unless you explicitly ask. It is a hosting tool, not a local development loop: there is no web UI, daemon, scheduler, webhook receiver, TLS terminator, database, or bundled reverse proxy, and a swap briefly stops the old container because the port is fixed.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ## Supported stacks
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z Support is claimed only for the stacks the integration suite builds and probes. Railpack may detect other projects, but that is not a support promise.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Stack | Verified fixture |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Vite/React static SPA | `fixtures/vite-spa` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Node/Express | `fixtures/express-api` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Python/FastAPI | `fixtures/fastapi-app` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z One repository produces one service. Multi-service and compose-style stacks are out of scope.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ## Prerequisites
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z easy-host targets Linux on x86_64 or arm64 and expects all of the following on the host:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Requirement | Minimum | Verify |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Rootless Podman | `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0` | `podman --version` and `podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'` (expect `true`) |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Lingering for the owning user | enabled | `loginctl show-user "$USER" -p Linger` (expect `Linger=yes`) |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | git | 2.40 or newer | `git --version` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | Node.js | 24 or newer | `node --version` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z | One free host port per app | 1024 or above | choose a free port and pass it with `--port` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z Three points are easy to miss:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z - **Podman 6.x is not supported.** The supported range is `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`; the 6.x major line is excluded while it is unstable. The `doctor` check fails on a version outside that range and names the supported range.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z - **Lingering is mandatory.** Without lingering, the user's systemd manager does not start at boot, so `--restart=always` containers do not come back after a reboot. Enable it with `sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"`. easy-host enables `podman-restart.service` on `add`, but that user unit can only replay containers once lingering has started the user manager.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z - **Privileged ports are unsupported.** Rootless Podman cannot bind a port below 1024 without a host-wide sysctl change, which easy-host does not make. Use port 1024 or above.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z Run `easy-host doctor` after installing. It checks Podman, rootless mode, a Docker-compatible image loader, lingering, reboot recovery, git, Node.js, Railpack, BuildKit, and disk, and every failing check prints a remediation command. Railpack exports images through a Docker-compatible loader; on the Ubuntu host used for the v0.1.0 release gate, the `podman-docker` package provided that loader. The step-by-step guide, including the Podman 4.9 upgrade path and a verification command for each requirement, is [Host prerequisites](docs/operations/prerequisites.md). The normative requirements and every check are in [Prerequisites and Doctor](docs/features/01-prerequisites-and-doctor.md); the verified host evidence is in the [v0.1.0 release-gate record](docs/reviews/v1-success-scenarios-evidence.md).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ## Install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z Install Node.js 24 or newer first. easy-host is not published to the npm registry; install it globally from a checkout by one of the three supported paths. Replace `<repository-url>` with the clone URL you use for this repository.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z **From a clone (current revision):**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z git clone <repository-url> easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z cd easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z npm install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z npm install -g .
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z **From a release tag (`v0.1.0`):**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z git clone --branch v0.1.0 <repository-url> easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z cd easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z npm install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z npm install -g .
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z **From a packed tarball:**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.732Z npm install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z npm pack
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z npm install -g ./easy-host-0.1.0.tgz
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z `npm install` installs the build dependencies, and the package's `prepare` script builds `dist/` before `npm pack` and when installing from a clone. The package is marked `private`, so there is no registry publish path.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z Do not use `npm install -g git+<repository-url>#v0.1.0` as the tag path. npm prepares a git dependency before its devDependencies are available, so that form fails to build; clone the tag and install from the checkout instead.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host keeps its state under `$EASY_HOST_HOME` when set, otherwise `$XDG_DATA_HOME/easy-host`, otherwise `~/.local/share/easy-host`, created with mode `0700`. Each app gets `apps/<name>/config.toml` and its own workspace; there is no database.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z Confirm the install with:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host version
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host doctor
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ## Quickstart
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z These five commands take a repository from clone to a healthy, self-hosted service. The example app name is `blog` and the host port is `8080`; choose a free port at or above 1024.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host doctor
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host add https://github.com/your-org/your-app.git --name blog --port 8080 --yes
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host status blog
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host logs blog --tail 100
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host update blog
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z `doctor` fails before the first `add` if the host is not ready. `add` clones the repository at the configured ref, builds the image, creates the container on `0.0.0.0:8080` by default, and waits for the readiness probe. The success summary prints the URL, image, previous image, and health result. `status` reports the container state, drift, port, and image; `logs` is a `podman logs` passthrough; `update` fetches the ref, rebuilds only when needed, and health-gates the swap.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z The app is reachable from another machine on the LAN at `http://<host-lan-address>:8080/`. easy-host publishes the port on the LAN; it does not terminate TLS or act as a reverse proxy, so internet exposure and HTTPS are the operator's responsibility.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host ships no scheduler. To repeat `update` on a schedule, write a systemd user timer that calls it; the [scheduled updates guide](docs/operations/systemd-timer.md) has complete unit files, enable commands, log location, and the lock behavior when runs overlap.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ## Success scenarios
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z The v0.1.0 release gate exercises the four outcomes below on a fresh Linux host with rootless Podman `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`, lingering enabled, and an empty state root. The [release-gate record](docs/reviews/v1-success-scenarios-evidence.md) contains the commands, exit codes, and observed output.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ### 1. The app is reachable from another machine
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host add https://github.com/your-org/your-app.git --name blog --port 8080 --yes
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z curl -fsS http://<host-lan-address>:8080/
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z The `add` exits `0` and the app answers on the published port from a second machine on the LAN. A request to the host's own loopback from that second machine is not expected to answer; use the host's LAN address.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ### 2. The app returns after a reboot
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z Reboot the host and wait for it to come back. With lingering enabled, easy-host has enabled `podman-restart.service`, which replays `--restart=always` containers at boot. No easy-host command is required, and the app answers on the same port.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ### 3. A broken update keeps the previous version serving
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z git push origin main
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z easy-host update blog
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:07.733Z ```
