[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z ## 20. Open Questions
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | # | Question | Default Assumption |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z |---|----------|--------------------|
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 1 | Which license? | MIT, declared in `LICENSE` and `package.json`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 2 | Should `config --edit` open `$EDITOR` and re-validate on save? | Yes: open `$EDITOR`, then validate and print errors without applying anything. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 3 | Should `add` accept repeatable `--env KEY=VALUE` flags in addition to `[env]` and the secret file? | Yes, for scripting; values land in the secret file, not in `config.toml`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 4 | Exact image tag format? | `localhost/easy-host-<app>:<UTC yyyymmddThhmmssZ>`; state records the two refs, no mutable `:current` tag. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 5 | Should `status` exit non-zero when any app is unhealthy? | Yes, exit 4, so timers and monitors can act on it. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 6 | Should `list` hide apps whose containers are missing? | No: show them as `missing` so drift is visible. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 7 | Should the tool enforce a minimum free disk threshold before building? | Warn below 5 GiB, fail below 2 GiB, both configurable in `doctor` output only (no config key in v1). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 8 | Should `update --rebuild` force a build even when the diff says config-only? | Yes; the flag exists for cache and Railpack-version changes. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 9 | Should `remove` offer to keep images for faster re-add? | No in v1; `remove` deletes images, `remove --keep-images` is a future consideration. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 10 | What is the exact `--json` schema version field? | `"schemaVersion": 1` on every JSON payload; bump only for breaking field changes. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 11 | Is a `restart` command needed despite the settled ten-command surface? | No; `update` without changes and `rollback` cover recovery, and Podman restart is the operator's tool. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 12 | Does v1 need shell completion generation at install time? | No; `easy-host completion <shell>` prints the script and docs explain where to place it. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z | 13 | When can Podman 6.x re-enter the supported range? | Not in v1. Re-evaluate after a stable 6.x release and a passing Phase 0 BuildKit spike on that version; until then `doctor` rejects 6.x and the docs point at the newest 5.8.x package. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=2 at=2026-10-30T20:48:19.825Z ---
