[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z === lock ===
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z /**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * Per-app and name-allocation locks (REG-FR-05).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * A mutating lifecycle operation takes one exclusive lock file inside the app
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * directory; `add` additionally takes a short-lived allocation lock beside the
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * apps directory while it re-checks the name and creates the directory. Both
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * locks record the holder's pid and start time so a conflict can name the
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * process that owns it.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * Acquire is non-blocking: the complete lock document is hard-linked into
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * place, and a live holder makes the second caller fail immediately with exit
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * code 6. A lock whose pid is gone is reclaimed. Reclamation renames the stale
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * file to a unique quarantine path and verifies the bytes have not changed in
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * the meantime, so a concurrent reclaim cannot delete a lock that a third
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * process just acquired.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  *
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * Read-only commands never take a lock: this module offers no global lock, and
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * callers acquire the app lock only around the mutation they perform. The
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * return value of {@link withAppLock} and {@link withAllocationLock} is the
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  * action's result; the lock is released in `finally` on every throw path.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:18.365Z  */
