[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.486Z # easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.486Z easy-host is a Linux CLI that turns a git repository into a long-running, self-hosted HTTP service on a single machine. It clones the repository, builds an image with Railpack (no per-repo Dockerfile), runs it under rootless Podman with `--restart=always` on one host port you declare, health-gates every update, keeps the last two images for rollback, and never deletes a named volume unless you explicitly ask. It is a hosting tool, not a local development loop: there is no web UI, daemon, scheduler, webhook receiver, TLS terminator, database, or bundled reverse proxy, and a swap briefly stops the old container because the port is fixed.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.486Z ## Supported stacks
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z Support is claimed only for the stacks the integration suite builds and probes. Railpack may detect other projects, but that is not a support promise.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Stack | Verified fixture |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Vite/React static SPA | `fixtures/vite-spa` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Node/Express | `fixtures/express-api` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Python/FastAPI | `fixtures/fastapi-app` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z One repository produces one service. Multi-service and compose-style stacks are out of scope.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z ## Prerequisites
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z easy-host targets Linux on x86_64 or arm64 and expects all of the following on the host:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Requirement | Minimum | Verify |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Rootless Podman | `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0` | `podman --version` and `podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'` (expect `true`) |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Lingering for the owning user | enabled | `loginctl show-user "$USER" -p Linger` (expect `Linger=yes`) |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | git | 2.40 or newer | `git --version` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | Node.js | 24 or newer | `node --version` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z | One free host port per app | 1024 or above | choose a free port and pass it with `--port` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z Three points are easy to miss:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z - **Podman 6.x is not supported.** The supported range is `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`; the 6.x major line is excluded while it is unstable. The `doctor` check fails on a version outside that range and names the supported range.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z - **Lingering is mandatory.** Without lingering, the user's systemd manager does not start at boot, so `--restart=always` containers do not come back after a reboot. Enable it with `sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"`. easy-host enables `podman-restart.service` on `add`, but that user unit can only replay containers once lingering has started the user manager.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z - **Privileged ports are unsupported.** Rootless Podman cannot bind a port below 1024 without a host-wide sysctl change, which easy-host does not make. Use port 1024 or above.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z Run `easy-host doctor` after installing. It checks Podman, rootless mode, a Docker-compatible image loader, lingering, reboot recovery, git, Node.js, Railpack, BuildKit, and disk, and every failing check prints a remediation command. Railpack exports images through a Docker-compatible loader; on the Ubuntu host used for the v0.1.0 release gate, the `podman-docker` package provided that loader. The step-by-step guide, including the Podman 4.9 upgrade path and a verification command for each requirement, is [Host prerequisites](docs/operations/prerequisites.md). The normative requirements and every check are in [Prerequisites and Doctor](docs/features/01-prerequisites-and-doctor.md); the verified host evidence is in the [v0.1.0 release-gate record](docs/reviews/v1-success-scenarios-evidence.md).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z ## Install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z Install Node.js 24 or newer first. easy-host is not published to the npm registry; install it globally from a checkout by one of the three supported paths. Replace `<repository-url>` with the clone URL you use for this repository.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z **From a clone (current revision):**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.490Z git clone <repository-url> easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z cd easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z npm install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z npm install -g .
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z **From a release tag (`v0.1.0`):**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z git clone --branch v0.1.0 <repository-url> easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z cd easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z npm install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z npm install -g .
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z **From a packed tarball:**
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z npm install
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z npm pack
