[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z `npm install` installs the build dependencies, and the package's `prepare` script builds `dist/` before `npm pack` and when installing from a clone. The package is marked `private`, so there is no registry publish path.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z Do not use `npm install -g git+<repository-url>#v0.1.0` as the tag path. npm prepares a git dependency before its devDependencies are available, so that form fails to build; clone the tag and install from the checkout instead.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:50:42.491Z easy-host keeps its state under `$EASY_HOST_HOME` when set, otherwise `$XDG_DATA_HOME/easy-host`, otherwise `~/.local/share/easy-host`, created with mode `0700`. Each app gets `apps/<name>/config.toml` and its own workspace; there is no database.
