[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z $ sed -n '139,154p' docs/operations/systemd-timer.md && git diff --check && git status --short
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z ## What each exit code means for the timer
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z `update` uses the stable exit-code contract documented in `docs/features/01-prerequisites-and-doctor.md`. systemd records any nonzero result as a failed unit, so the number in the journal tells you whether the schedule, the host, the source, or the app needs attention.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | Exit | Meaning for `easy-host update blog` | What to do |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `0` | Success: the app was updated and is healthy, or nothing changed (a no-op). | None. For a git-backed app, a no-op still fetches the configured ref, so a scheduled run notices a moved commit. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `1` | Usage or validation failure: app name that fails the name pattern, unsupported flag, or invalid `config.toml`. | Fix the `ExecStart` line or the app configuration; the timer is misconfigured, not unlucky. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `2` | Prerequisite or environment failure: state root not writable, container engine unavailable, or the environment file could not be read. | Run `easy-host doctor`, fix the failing check, then retry once by hand. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `3` | Fetch or build failure. The serving container and `config.toml` were not touched. | Inspect the build output in the journal. Fix the commit or build inputs; the next scheduled run retries. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `4` | Readiness failure. The candidate did not become healthy; when a previous image exists, it is serving again with `state: reverted`. | Inspect `easy-host logs blog --tail 200` and the probe line in the journal. The previous version keeps serving. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `5` | App not found: `blog` was removed, renamed, or mistyped in `ExecStart`. | Disable the timer, or correct the app name in `ExecStart`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `6` | Conflict or lock held: another mutation of `blog` is running, or a declared port or volume conflicts with another app. | If it coincides with another run, ignore it; the next trigger is fine. If it repeats with no overlapping run, inspect the error block for `PORT_CONFLICT`, `VOLUME_NAME_CONFLICT`, or `LOCK_HELD`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z | `7` | Unexpected internal error. | Re-run with `EASY_HOST_DEBUG=1` in the unit environment and capture the journal output for a bug report. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.4 attempt=3 at=2026-10-30T20:51:35.341Z The human error block in the journal is the same one you see in a terminal: a summary line, structured detail lines, and a `next:` remediation. Use that remediation before changing the schedule.
