[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z # easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ## 1. Overview
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z **Product Name:** easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z **Summary:** A Linux CLI that turns a git repository into a long-running, self-hosted HTTP service on one machine. It clones the repo, builds an image with Railpack (no per-repo Dockerfile), runs it under rootless Podman with a restart policy on a port the operator declares, health-gates every update, keeps the last two images for rollback, and removes apps without ever deleting data by accident.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z **Target Platform:** Linux only (x86_64 and arm64), rootless Podman `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`, Node.js 24 or newer, system git 2.40 or newer.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z **Key Constraints:** Single host; CLI only; one explicit host port per app bound on the LAN by default; no TLS, no bundled reverse proxy, no database, no daemon, no scheduler; secrets are plain `0600` files; observability is `podman logs` passthrough only.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z This document is the authoritative product definition. Feature-level requirements, task contracts, and acceptance details live in [docs/features/](features/). Source material for this version: [IDEA.md](IDEA.md).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ---
