[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ## 3. Goals and Non-Goals
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ### 3.1 Goals
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z - Make the path from "I have a repo" to "it is a service that survives reboot" a single command with no container authoring.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z - Guarantee that a bad deploy does not take the service down: the previous version keeps or regains serving.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z - Make rollback a one-command operation with a predictable two-image window.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z - Keep the operator's data safe: no command deletes a declared volume unless explicitly asked.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z - Stay small enough for one person to operate and reason about: a plain on-disk registry, no database, no control plane.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z - Be honest about support: only stacks exercised by the integration suite are claimed.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ```forge-requirement
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z {"id":"PRD-C-01","kind":"constraint","text":"The product surface is a command-line interface only. No web UI, dashboard, HTTP API, or desktop application ships in v1."}
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ```forge-requirement
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z {"id":"PRD-C-02","kind":"constraint","text":"Run on a single Linux host with rootless Podman >= 5.7.0 and < 6.0.0. Podman 6.x is excluded while that major line is unstable. No multi-node operation, scheduling, clustering, or orchestrator integration."}
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z === SEC20 ===
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ## 20. Open Questions
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | # | Question | Default Assumption |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z |---|----------|--------------------|
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 1 | Which license? | MIT, declared in `LICENSE` and `package.json`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 2 | Should `config --edit` open `$EDITOR` and re-validate on save? | Yes: open `$EDITOR`, then validate and print errors without applying anything. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 3 | Should `add` accept repeatable `--env KEY=VALUE` flags in addition to `[env]` and the secret file? | Yes, for scripting; values land in the secret file, not in `config.toml`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 4 | Exact image tag format? | `localhost/easy-host-<app>:<UTC yyyymmddThhmmssZ>`; state records the two refs, no mutable `:current` tag. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 5 | Should `status` exit non-zero when any app is unhealthy? | Yes, exit 4, so timers and monitors can act on it. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 6 | Should `list` hide apps whose containers are missing? | No: show them as `missing` so drift is visible. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 7 | Should the tool enforce a minimum free disk threshold before building? | Warn below 5 GiB, fail below 2 GiB, both configurable in `doctor` output only (no config key in v1). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 8 | Should `update --rebuild` force a build even when the diff says config-only? | Yes; the flag exists for cache and Railpack-version changes. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 9 | Should `remove` offer to keep images for faster re-add? | No in v1; `remove` deletes images, `remove --keep-images` is a future consideration. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 10 | What is the exact `--json` schema version field? | `"schemaVersion": 1` on every JSON payload; bump only for breaking field changes. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 11 | Is a `restart` command needed despite the settled ten-command surface? | No; `update` without changes and `rollback` cover recovery, and Podman restart is the operator's tool. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 12 | Does v1 need shell completion generation at install time? | No; `easy-host completion <shell>` prints the script and docs explain where to place it. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | 13 | When can Podman 6.x re-enter the supported range? | Not in v1. Re-evaluate after a stable 6.x release and a passing Phase 0 BuildKit spike on that version; until then `doctor` rejects 6.x and the docs point at the newest 5.8.x package. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ---
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z ## 21. Glossary
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Term | Definition |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z |------|------------|
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | App | One repository (or local path) turned into one container and one host port, tracked under a unique name. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | AppSpec | The typed contents of an app's `config.toml`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | BuildKit | The builder Railpack drives to produce OCI images. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Current image | The image the running container was created from. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Drift | A difference between recorded state and Podman reality (missing container, wrong image, unhealthy probe). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Health gate | The rule that a candidate version must pass its probe before it replaces the serving version. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Lingering | The systemd setting that keeps a user's services (and rootless Podman containers) alive after logout and across reboot. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Previous image | The last image that served before the current one; the rollback target. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Railpack | The MIT build-detection tool that turns a repo into an image without a Dockerfile. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Registry | The on-disk `apps/` directory tree; the authoritative list of configured apps. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | Rootless Podman | Podman running entirely in a user namespace without root privileges. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.186Z | State cache | Per-app `state.json` holding image refs, last health result, and timestamps; rebuildable. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.187Z | Swap | The update/rollback sequence that stops the old container, starts the candidate, and probes it. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:27.187Z | Volume | A named Podman volume declared in config and mounted into the container at a declared path. |
