[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.822Z # CLI reference
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.822Z `easy-host` is a Linux CLI for running a git repository as a long-running service under rootless Podman. This page is the complete command, flag, argument, and exit-code reference. It is checked against the built commander program by `tests/docs/reference.test.ts`, so a command or flag that is added to the CLI without a matching entry here fails the test suite (`DOC-FR-04`, `DOC-NF-01`).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z The supported host range, the lingering requirement, and the port floor are in [Host prerequisites](../operations/prerequisites.md). The `config.toml` keys are in the [configuration reference](config.md). The command surface is also summarized in [PRD §12.1](../PRD.md#121-command-surface).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ## Synopsis
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z easy-host <command> [arguments] [options]
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z There are exactly ten commands: `add`, `list`, `status`, `logs`, `update`, `rollback`, `remove`, `config`, `doctor`, and `version`. There is no `start`, `stop`, `restart`, `prune`, `completion`, or `daemon` command, and easy-host ships no scheduler, webhook receiver, TLS terminator, or reverse proxy.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z The host baseline is rootless Podman `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0` (6.x is excluded while that major line is unstable), user lingering enabled with `sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"`, git 2.40 or newer, Node.js 24 or newer, and one free host port per app in the range 1024 to 65535. Privileged ports are unsupported.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | Command | Purpose | Mutates host state |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`add`](#add) | Clone or register an app, build it, and start its container | Yes |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`list`](#list) | List registered apps in one table | No |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`status`](#status) | Show one app or every app in detail | No |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`logs`](#logs) | Stream an app's container logs | No |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`update`](#update) | Rebuild or recreate an app behind a health gate | Yes |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`rollback`](#rollback) | Swap back to the previous image | Yes |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`remove`](#remove) | Delete an app, keeping volumes unless asked | Yes |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`config`](#config) | Show, validate, or edit an app's configuration | No (the editor writes the file) |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`doctor`](#doctor) | Check the host prerequisites | No |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | [`version`](#version) | Print the easy-host version | No |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z Commands without a mutating effect never take the app lock. Each mutating command takes the per-app lock and exits `6` when another easy-host process holds it.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ## Global options
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | Flag | Value | Default | Meaning |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--json` | none | off | Write one machine-readable JSON document to stdout. Accepted before or after any command. `list`, `status`, `config`, `doctor`, and `version` always emit a `schemaVersion: 1` success document. `add`, `update`, `rollback`, and `remove` emit the `schemaVersion: 1` error envelope on failure but keep their human success summary. `logs` is a passthrough and ignores `--json`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `-h`, `--help` | none | off | Print help for the program or for one command, then exit `0`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z Machine-readable results go to stdout. Progress, warnings, and human error text go to stderr, so `--json` output can be piped. Human output contains no ANSI escapes when stdout is not a terminal, when `NO_COLOR` is set, or when `TERM=dumb`; status meaning is always carried by text, never by colour alone.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ## Exit codes
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z Every expected failure maps to one code. Unexpected exceptions exit `7` with a bug-report hint instead of a raw stack trace. Set `EASY_HOST_DEBUG=1` to include diagnostics and the stack trace.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | Code | Name | Meaning |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `0` | success | The command completed. A no-op `update` is still success. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `1` | usage | Invalid arguments, invalid or missing configuration, a missing required flag, or a rejected flag combination. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `2` | prerequisite | A missing or unusable host prerequisite: Podman, rootless mode, lingering, git, Node.js, disk, state root, or the container runtime. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `3` | build | A clone, Railpack, or BuildKit failure. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `4` | health | A readiness probe failed, or `status` found an app that is unhealthy, stopped, or missing. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `5` | not found | The requested app, image, config file, or container does not exist. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `6` | conflict | A name, port, or volume conflict, or another process holds the app lock (`LOCK_HELD`). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `7` | internal | An unexpected exception. Re-run with `EASY_HOST_DEBUG=1` and report it. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z The human error block has three parts: a one-line summary, indented details, and a `next:` remediation command. Secret values and URL credentials are redacted in both human and JSON output.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ## Commands
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ### add
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z Create an app from a git repository or a local workspace, build its image, create its named volumes, start its container with `--restart=always`, and wait for the readiness probe.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ```text
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z easy-host add [git-url] [options]
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z #### Arguments
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | Argument | Required | Meaning |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `git-url` | No, unless `--local` is omitted | HTTPS, SSH, git, `git+ssh`, or `file://` repository URL, or an scp-style `user@host:path` remote. In an interactive terminal, omitting both sources prompts for one; a non-interactive run fails with exit `1`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z Exactly one of `git-url` and `--local` must be supplied. Supplying both is a usage error.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z #### Options
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | Flag | Value | Default | Meaning |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--local <path>` | path | none | Add a local workspace in place instead of cloning a repository. Local mode is dev-only and is not tracked by easy-host. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--name <app>` | string | derived from the source basename | App name. Must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$`; an existing name is a conflict (`6`). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--ref <ref>` | string | `main` | Git branch, tag, or commit to build. Ignored in local mode. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--port <port>` | integer | required, no default | Host port to publish. Must be 1024 to 65535 and unused by another app. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--container-port <port>` | integer | `3000` | Container port the app listens on. Must be 1024 to 65535. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--bind <addr>` | `0.0.0.0`, `127.0.0.1`, or `::` | `0.0.0.0` | Address the published host port binds to. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--env-file <path>` | path | `secrets.env` | App-relative environment file. Must stay inside the app directory and contain no `..` segment. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--health-path <path>` | HTTP path | `/` | Path requested by the readiness probe. Must start with `/`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--probe <http\|tcp>` | `http` or `tcp` | `http` | Readiness probe type. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--volume <name:container-path>` | `name:path` | none | Named volume to mount. Repeatable. The name must match `^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$` and the container path must be absolute and not `/`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--yes` | none | off | Never prompt. A missing required value fails with exit `1` instead of asking. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `--json` | none | off | Write the JSON error envelope on failure; success keeps the human summary. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z The readiness probe allows 90 seconds by default, with a 2-second interval and a 5-second per-attempt timeout. These values come from `health_startup_ms`, `health_interval_ms`, and `health_timeout_ms` in `config.toml`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z #### Examples
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z easy-host add https://github.com/your-org/blog.git --name blog --port 8080 --yes
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z easy-host add https://github.com/your-org/blog.git --ref v1.2.0 --port 8080 --volume data:/var/lib/data --yes
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z easy-host add --local ../blog --name blog --port 8081 --probe tcp
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z #### Exit codes
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | Code | When |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.823Z | `0` | The app is running and the probe succeeded. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.824Z | `1` | Invalid or missing input, invalid config, privileged or duplicate port, invalid name, or a bad volume declaration. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.824Z | `2` | A host prerequisite or container runtime check failed. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.824Z | `3` | The clone, Railpack build, or BuildKit export failed. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.824Z | `4` | The container started but the readiness probe failed. The container is removed and the image and app directory are kept. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:37.824Z | `6` | The app name, container name, volume name, or port is already claimed, or another process holds a lock. |
