[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 3:Each app is described by one TOML file at `<state-root>/apps/<name>/config.toml`. The file is written by `easy-host add` and can be edited by hand or with `easy-host config <app> --edit`. It is the authoritative definition of an app: `state.json` is only a rebuildable cache.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 7:The enclosing state root and file modes are covered in [Files and permissions](#files-and-permissions). Command behaviour is in the [CLI reference](cli.md).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 11:The state root resolves in this order:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 13:1. `EASY_HOST_HOME` when set and non-empty;
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 21:| `config.toml` | The validated app configuration documented on this page. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 96:1. the inline `[env]` table in `config.toml`;
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 117:| `<state-root>/` and its `apps/`, `tools/`, `buildkit/` children | `0700` | Created on first use and private to the operator. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 118:| `<state-root>/apps/<app>/` and `workspace/` | `0700` | App and checkout directories are private. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 119:| `<state-root>/apps/<app>/config.toml` | `0644` | Atomically replaced through a same-directory temporary file and rename. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 120:| `<state-root>/apps/<app>/secrets.env` | `0600` | Read-only secret input; easy-host never writes secret values into `config.toml`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 123:`config.toml`, `secrets.env`, and `state.json` writes are atomic: a crash leaves either the previous complete file or the new complete file, never a partial document. Comments on retained keys and table entries are preserved when easy-host rewrites the file.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z 131:| TOML syntax error | `invalid config.toml: <reason>`, with the source line and column where the parser reports them. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z === prereqs top ===
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z # Host prerequisites
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z easy-host runs on a Linux host that is already prepared for rootless containers. This guide lists every prerequisite, the command that proves it on your host, and the check that enforces it — a `doctor` check where one exists, and the `add`/`update` preflight for the per-app port rule. Run the checks before the first `add`; a missing prerequisite fails during `doctor` instead of after a long build.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z The command that checks the host before the first `add` is:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.453Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z easy-host doctor
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z `doctor` exits `0` when every check passes or warns, and exits `2` when any check fails. Each failing line is followed by a `next:` remediation. It reads only local state and never installs or downloads anything. The full check list and its output contract are in the Prerequisites and Doctor feature document (`docs/features/01-prerequisites-and-doctor.md`).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ## Summary
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | Prerequisite | Required value | Verify with | Doctor check |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | --- | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | Rootless Podman | `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0` | `podman --version` and `podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'` | `podman`, `podman-rootless` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | User lingering | `Linger=yes` for the owning user | `loginctl show-user "$USER" -p Linger` | `linger` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | Boot replay unit | `podman-restart.service` enabled | `systemctl --user is-enabled podman-restart.service` | `boot-restart` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | git | 2.40 or newer | `git --version` | `git` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | Node.js | 24 or newer | `node --version` | `node` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | Docker-compatible image loader | `docker --version` succeeds | `docker --version` | `docker-loader` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | One free host port per app | 1024 to 65535, unused, unique per app | `ss -ltnH "sport = :8080"` (empty output means free) | None by design (no host-wide check); the `add` and `update` preflight validates it |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z | Free disk space | 2 GiB minimum; 5 GiB recommended | `df -h "$HOME"` | `disk` |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z The remaining doctor checks, `railpack` and `buildkit`, cover the build tooling that easy-host installs on first use. They are described under [Other doctor checks](#other-doctor-checks).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z If you set `EASY_HOST_HOME` to a directory on another filesystem, measure that filesystem with `df -h "$EASY_HOST_HOME"`; the `disk` doctor check always measures the filesystem that actually holds the state root.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ## Rootless Podman
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z easy-host requires **rootless** Podman in the range `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`. Run easy-host as your normal user, never with `sudo`: a rootful Podman is unsupported even when its version is in range.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ### Check the host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z podman --version
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z The first command must print `5.7.0` or newer in the 5.x line. The second must print `true`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z - `podman` is the doctor check for presence and version. It fails when Podman is missing, below `5.7.0`, or at or above `6.0.0`. When it can read a version, it names the found version and the supported range.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z - `podman-rootless` is the doctor check for rootless mode. It fails when `podman info` reports `false` or the call fails, and tells you to run as a normal user. When Podman itself is missing, this check is skipped because the `podman` check has already failed.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z `5.7.0` and `5.8.9` rootless are covered by the doctor unit tests; the v0.1.0 release gate ran `5.7.0` rootless. Any later 5.x release is accepted, because the upper bound is the exclusive `6.0.0`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ### Why 4.9 and 6.x are excluded
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z - **Podman 4.9.3 is out of security support** and is the package shipped by stock Ubuntu 24.04 and Debian 12. Supporting it would mean owning rootless BuildKit defects on an unmaintained runtime, so it is below the hard minimum. This is the platform finding recorded in PRD §5.4.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z - **Podman 6.x is excluded while that major line is unstable.** The supported window stops at `6.0.0` (exclusive). A 6.x host is rejected even if the version number looks newer. Re-entering 6.x requires a stable release and a passing rootless BuildKit spike, so there is no flag, environment variable, or config key that opts in early. `doctor` reports the found version and a downgrade starting point.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z - **Every version below 5.7.0 fails**, including 4.9.3. `doctor` exits `2` and names both the found version and `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ### Upgrade from Podman 4.9 on Ubuntu 24.04
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z Ubuntu 24.04's archive carries Podman 4.9.3, which fails the minimum. Doctor's Ubuntu remediation names two starting points: the newest Podman 5.8.x package from Ubuntu 25.04+ or the upstream Podman PPA. The goal is to replace 4.9.3 with 5.7.0 or newer in the 5.x line, then prove it with `podman --version`. The exact 5.x version in a distribution point release is not pinned by easy-host, so verify it after the upgrade rather than assuming it.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z 1. Record what you are leaving:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z $ cd /home/mcfuzzysquirrel/Projects/react-hoster/.forge-sandboxes/DOC-1.6 && sed -n '60,130p' docs/operations/prerequisites.md && echo "=== path code ===" && sed -n '75,130p' src/platform/paths.ts
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    podman --version
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    # podman version 4.9.3
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z 2. Move the host to a source that carries 5.7.0 or newer. Either upgrade the Ubuntu release to a currently supported release at or above the doctor's named floor (25.04), or add the upstream Podman PPA using that PPA's own published instructions for your release. Do not point `apt` at a source this guide has not named.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z 3. With the newer source configured, upgrade the package:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    sudo apt update
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    sudo apt install --only-upgrade podman
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z 4. Verify the result and re-run doctor:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    podman --version
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    easy-host doctor
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z    ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z If step 4 lands on a 6.x release, stop and downgrade to the newest 5.8.x package from the same source. easy-host will not accept 6.x. If the named source still installs a version below 5.7.0, that source does not satisfy the prerequisite; use the upstream Podman packages for your distribution instead of assuming the distro release is enough.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z This upgrade was not replayed on this project's release-gate host; that host already ran Podman 5.7.0. The source choices above are the ones the `doctor` remediation names. The verification steps are the part you must run yourself.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.454Z ### Upgrade from Podman 4.9 on Debian 12
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z Debian 12's archive also carries Podman 4.9.3. Doctor's Debian remediation names Debian 13 (trixie) or newer as the starting point. The goal is the same: replace 4.9.3 with 5.7.0 or newer in the 5.x line and prove it with `podman --version`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z 1. Record what you are leaving:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    podman --version
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    # podman version 4.9.3
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z 2. Upgrade the host to Debian 13 (trixie) or newer, the starting point the doctor names, then check the version its archive actually provides.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z 3. Install the newer package and verify:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    sudo apt update
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    sudo apt install --only-upgrade podman
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    podman --version
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    podman info --format '{{.Host.Security.Rootless}}'
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    easy-host doctor
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z    ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z There is no documented in-place path for staying on Debian 12: its own package is 4.9.3 and no Debian 12 backport of Podman 5.7 was verified for this release. Do not install an unverified third-party package to avoid the distro upgrade. If Debian 13's archive still installs a version below 5.7.0, use the upstream Podman packages for Debian instead.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ### If you are already on Podman 6.x
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z `doctor` fails the `podman` check with the found 6.x version and tells you to downgrade to the newest 5.8.x package. That is intentional: the support window is `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`, and the build layer has not been spiked against a stable 6.x line. Downgrade rather than looking for an override.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ## User lingering
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z Lingering is **mandatory**, not a convenience. Without it, systemd does not start a user manager for your account at boot, so no user unit runs. `podman-restart.service` is a user unit, so a container with `--restart=always` does not come back after a reboot; the app stays down until you log in or start it by hand.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ### Check and enable
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z loginctl show-user "$USER" -p Linger
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z Expected output: `Linger=yes`. If it prints `Linger=no`, enable it once:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ```sh
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z sudo loginctl enable-linger "$USER"
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z ```
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:41.455Z === path code ===
