[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z # Configuration reference
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z Each app is described by one TOML file at `<state-root>/apps/<name>/config.toml`. The file is written by `easy-host add` and can be edited by hand or with `easy-host config <app> --edit`. It is the authoritative definition of an app: `state.json` is only a rebuildable cache.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z This page documents every key, type, default, and validation rule, the volumes table, and the environment precedence order. `tests/docs/reference.test.ts` imports `APP_SPEC_KEYS` and `APP_SPEC_DEFAULTS` from `src/config/schema.ts` and fails when a schema key or default is missing here (`DOC-FR-04`, `DOC-NF-01`).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z The enclosing state root and file modes are covered in [Files and permissions](#files-and-permissions). Command behaviour is in the [CLI reference](cli.md).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z ## Location
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z The state root resolves in this order:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z 1. `EASY_HOST_HOME` when set and non-empty;
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z 2. `$XDG_DATA_HOME/easy-host` when `XDG_DATA_HOME` is set;
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z 3. `~/.local/share/easy-host`.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z An app lives at `<state-root>/apps/<app>/` and contains:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z | Entry | Purpose |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.717Z | `config.toml` | The validated app configuration documented on this page. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z | `secrets.env` | Optional secret values, by default. Selected by the `env_file` key. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z | `workspace/` | The cloned repository, or a local path used in place for a dev-only app. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z | `state.json` | Rebuildable cache of image references, health, and timestamps. Never authoritative. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z ## Minimal config
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z ```toml
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z # The repository is cloned at add time and fetched again by update.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z repo = "https://github.com/your-org/blog.git"
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z # The only key with no default. Rootless Podman cannot publish below 1024.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z port = 8080
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z # Optional, shown with their defaults:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z ref = "main"
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z container_port = 3000
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z bind = "0.0.0.0"
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z probe = "http"
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:57:51.718Z health_path = "/"
