[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z # Migration from react-hoster to easy-host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z The project is now **easy-host**; the previous name was **react-hoster**. The repository is still named `react-hoster` in this checkout. Renaming the repository is a manual step outside this work, so the clone URL and directory name do not change until it is performed by hand. This note does not claim that the repository rename has happened.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z The [README](../README.md) is the current operator entry point, the [product definition](PRD.md) is the authoritative scope, and the [version history](PRD.md#2-version-history) records the Podman re-baseline in v1.1.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z ## What the old README claimed
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z The old README contained only:
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z > # react-hoster
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z >
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z > A podman container you can load your react app in and self host
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z It described a Podman container for a React app. It did not document an install command, a binary name, a supported-stack list, a config file or location, host prerequisites, updates, rollback, or volume handling.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z ## What an existing user must change
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z | Area | Old README | easy-host |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z | --- | --- | --- |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z | Install command | Not documented | Clone the repository and run `npm install`, then `npm install -g .`, with Node.js 24 or newer. See [Install](../README.md#install). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z | Binary name | `react-hoster` appeared only as the project heading; no command was documented | `easy-host`, for example `easy-host doctor`. |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z | Config location | Not documented | `<state-root>/apps/<app>/config.toml`, where the state root is `$EASY_HOST_HOME`, else `$XDG_DATA_HOME/easy-host`, else `~/.local/share/easy-host`. See [Location](reference/config.md#location). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z | Podman minimum | Not stated | Rootless Podman `>= 5.7.0, < 6.0.0`; the 6.x line is excluded while it is unstable and must be downgraded. See [Host prerequisites](operations/prerequisites.md#rootless-podman). |
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z The old README documented no on-disk state, so there is no automatic conversion step to run. Start new apps with `easy-host add` so they are recorded in the state root above.
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z ## Behavior that differs
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z - easy-host is a CLI for a git repository, not a React-only container. Only Vite/React, Node/Express, and Python/FastAPI are claimed as supported; see [Supported stacks](../README.md#supported-stacks).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z - Updates are health-gated, the last two images are kept for rollback, and `remove` never deletes a named volume unless `--volumes` is passed. See the [CLI reference](reference/cli.md) and [Volume safety](../README.md#volume-safety).
[engine] harness activity stderr task=DOC-1.6 attempt=1 at=2026-10-30T20:58:56.903Z - easy-host ships no daemon, scheduler, webhook receiver, TLS terminator, or reverse proxy. A schedule is a systemd user timer that calls `easy-host update`; see [Scheduled updates](operations/systemd-timer.md).
